WEBVTT

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:11.770
Bearers of Magic Eyes all across the continent are gathering,

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.530
and it appears that they're forming an anti-Gastark movement.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.290
The one behind it is most likely...

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.650
Come on out.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.390
Y-You!

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.660
I-I'm sorry for coming in without permission.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.810
There were so many pretty jewels... They caught my eye.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.580
The things here wouldn't look good on you.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:37.550
If you'd like some jewelry, I'll buy you whatever you like.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.020
I have no reason to accept anything from you!

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.290
Having second thoughts?

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:41.100
No, I never liked this country much anyway.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:46.050
I meant to ask if you were looking back to the time when you were human.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.010
Were human?

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:53.590
Ryner, we're not humans, inferior creatures.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.570
We are superior beings that bear the Eyes of God.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:01.220
You like humans, don't you?

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:05.920
But you must understand by now that we can't coexist with them.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.920
No matter how much you seek it, they won't give you that.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.410
The closer you grow, the more it hurts.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:18.710
You don't have to agonize over it any longer. You're not alone.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.180
Let's go. Our friends are waiting.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:37.700
This is...

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.960
The outer texture is dry, and your teeth don't sink into it properly.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.060
It's neither sweet, nor salty.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.820
The stench of our old flour overwhelms the senses!

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.530
Damn you, Ryner!

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.580
If only he were here...

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.920
I'd force this dumpling down his throat as punishment!

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.890
It's dull being alone.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.690
Come, let us be off. Our friends are waiting.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:13.100
Ryner...

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.190
Ryner!

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.140
<i>Aren't...</i>

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:25.580
<i>Aren't I... your friend?</i>

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.590
Miss! Your luggage!

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.530
Just what is this all about?

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:45.050
Their existence is a danger capable of destroying entire countries!

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:49.160
The Alpha Stigma is an existence which holds incredible magical power.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:53.080
In the era of the prior king, he underwent special training,

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.310
and was even referred to as Roland's most powerful magician.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.440
Roland's most powerful magician, you say?!

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.940
You mean to say the Alpha Stigma, when put to proper use, can be of great military aid?

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:07.780
Of course, since he was an Alpha Stigma bearer,

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.240
and was in constant danger of going out of control,

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.120
I had the Taboo Breaker Pursuit Squadron monitor his movements.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.250
With orders to kill him on the spot, should he go out of control.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.010
It was all for the sake of this country.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.510
I see. When you put it that way...

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.150
Keeping a monster in our ranks...

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.170
Our king is truly impressive!

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.540
No monster would pose a problem for him.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:31.580
Indeed.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.980
Ryner was right. You're not to blame.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.230
You're wrong.

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:48.080
Neither of you are to blame.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:49.500
You're wrong.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:53.470
I won't cause any more trouble for you.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:57.700
It must be rough, looking after a monster who could go out of control at any moment.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.290
You're wrong, Ryner!

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:07.680
I... I now know the reason why I can't reach you.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.840
So, Ryner, join me.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:14.840
What a farce.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:20.220
I held out my hand to you myself, and I ruined it all myself.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:28.190
You've grown into a sweet child. That alone makes me proud.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.540
You're wrong, Mother.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:34.830
I'm not sweet. I'm nothing to be proud of.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.540
That's why I'm all alone.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.790
I utterly refuse to accept it!

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:52.370
Calm down, Lize.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.680
We haven't even covered the specifics yet!

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:57.250
That won't be necessary!

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.790
What's the meaning of this?!

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:06.860
I utterly refuse to accept His Majesty joining this woman in marriage!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.940
What? Marriage?

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:09.580
Nice!

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.910
It looks as good on you as I'd hoped, Kiefer.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:17.290
What's the big idea? Where did you put my clothes?

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:21.670
Well, you heard me, everyone. I'll be marrying her.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.170
And that's that.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:24.540
Huh?!

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.430
So he's finally decided to settle down...

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:28.780
Gastark should be more stable as well...

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:29.530
But is this sudden decision safe?
Gastark should be more stable as well...

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:30.670
But is this sudden decision safe?

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.490
I don't know what country she fought for,

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:36.720
but I cannot allow a woman of such unknown lineage to be placed at your side!

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:41.430
I don't remember accepting any marriage with you, either!

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:44.000
Then give me the okay now.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.230
Quit joking!

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.500
Your Majesty! Would you just...?

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.810
Help, Riphal!

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.740
Brother Sui... Brother Sui is...

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:00.210
What happened?!

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.120
How awful.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.040
I'm all right.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.710
You should make Kuu get some rest.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.740
She's used the scythe's power this whole time...

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:16.480
...to carry me all the way here...

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:18.210
Prepare for an operation. Hurry!

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:18.860
Sir!

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.210
Who on earth would have...?

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.460
Forget about that for now.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:25.650
Don't speak, Sui. I'll be sure to save you, okay?

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.530
N-No, I'll speak.

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:32.900
This might be the last time I can...

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.320
Brother Sui!

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.230
Don't be ridiculous! There's no way I'm letting you die!

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.740
Lize, please...

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.650
Your Majesty, your decision?

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:50.290
Take Kuu.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.210
You've struggled hard.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.720
Get plenty of rest now.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.290
Thank you.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.410
<i>This is how strong this country is.</i>

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.410
<i>Its servants gladly cast away their lives for their king.</i>

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:18.530
<i>And the king sacrifices his own body to progress forward.</i>

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:23.240
What happened in the south, to cause such wounds?

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:26.360
A man using a Rule Fragment...

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:30.370
The same type as brother Lir's Lighting Beast Ring...

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:33.020
What country was he from?

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:34.440
I don't know.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.990
And, in Roland...

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.890
They have a monster named Ryner Lute lending them power.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:46.670
He looks like any ordinary Alpha Stigma bearer.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:50.250
But I've never seen such a monster...

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.690
Riphal, figure out what he is...

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.530
Your Majesty.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:03.870
It would appear that this woman is familiar with the name Ryner Lute.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:26.980
You're not eating?

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:30.150
Do you not like them?

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.360
No, I hate dumplings.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.980
Is it that hard accepting that you're not human?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.570
Your misfortunes begin at birth.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:46.740
You're born as a human child, and as you're raised, you get brainwashed.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:51.290
You love people, devote yourselves to them, yet you always end up betrayed.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.830
Isn't it the same for you?

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:58.590
No. The timing of the eye opening is different for my lino Doue.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.550
The lino Doue eye opening occurs before one is born,

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:05.760
while in a human woman's stomach.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:10.010
A voice became clear to me. A voice that only I could hear.

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:13.340
Everything... is yours to toy with.

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:18.610
Release it. Open up. Kill... everything.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:21.040
That voice commanded me.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:25.870
It told me to have my first feeding, to devour that inferior human.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:27.240
So, I'm...

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.880
Do you think of me as a monster, too?

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:39.960
No.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.320
Right now,

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:44.780
the sensibilities you developed growing up might still be hindering you.

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:47.190
But we are superior beings.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:51.890
A separate species, with power far beyond that of humans.

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.490
Frankly, I still find the whole thing unbelievable.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.210
Sir Sion, keeping an Alpha Stigma bearer on a leash?

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:17.410
Alpha Stigma, huh?

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:21.050
Don't most of those guys go out of control as kids and wind up dead?

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.250
Yes. But Ryner Lute seems to be an unusual type,

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:27.670
one who returns back to normal after going out of control.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:29.670
Ryner Lute.

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:34.140
His real name, actual age, birthplace, and everything else are all unclear.

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:37.860
At an age presumed to be five, he was taken into a bandit village.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.980
There it was discovered that he had an Alpha Stigma,

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:41.560
and he was taken into military custody.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:46.230
At the Germer Kleisrole Training Institute, he underwent combat training,

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:51.120
and after that, he was sent to Roland Special Training Institute #307.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.410
He underwent the deadliest of training,

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:57.450
and was then placed in a Roland military secret organization.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:02.910
They dubbed him Roland's strongest magician.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:07.360
But he doesn't seem to have handled missions well.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:11.220
Mission abandonment and obstruction, leaking of secret information,

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.180
insubordination to military higher-ups...

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:16.180
So they partly had surveillance in mind

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:18.400
when they dumped him in the Royal Special Academy.

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.820
Yes. That's where he met Sir Sion.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:26.270
It's amazing that he never betrayed Roland before this.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:31.550
In the old days, I saw a lot of people like him.

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:33.910
After going through one horrible experience after another,

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.440
they try to resign themselves to it all by going completely emotionally dead.

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:42.440
After all, nothing will be changed. Nothing can be changed.

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.550
It all sucks. None of it matters.

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:50.690
Guess I wouldn't know how a monster feels, though.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.110
That's the place?

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:00.250
It's temporary lodgings.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.890
We plan to move out in another few days.

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:05.650
Brother Tiir!

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.120
A kid?

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:08.970
You took too long, Tiir!

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:10.580
We've been waiting so long for you!

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.120
Tiir!

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:13.900
Sorry, sorry.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.020
Have you been good children while I've been out?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:16.930
Yeah, I've been extra good!

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:18.280
Where did you go?
Yeah, I've been extra good!

00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:19.130
Yeah, I've been extra good!

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.230
Here you go.

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:26.610
T-Thanks.

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:30.210
What a surprise. Are they all...?

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:34.780
Yes. They all bear the Eyes of God.

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:37.260
They're chased by humans, given nowhere to go.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.270
And they're hunted down.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:46.830
Lightning Beasts!

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:49.910
Stop!

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:57.800
Whoops! Even an lino Doue can't consume my Lightning Beasts.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:02.890
Geez, brother Lir. If you kill him, we won't be able to steal the crystal!

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:04.760
This will be our seventy-sixth!

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:09.130
Monster extermination safely complete, huh?

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:17.510
Thirty-eight people were killed then.

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:22.130
Who are the real monsters here?

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.730
They said they were from Gastark.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:27.440
Gastark...

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.950
I will make Gastark pay.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:34.020
Those lowly humans dared to meddle with us.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:36.150
I'll make them regret it one day.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:41.910
Tiir, I'm hungry!

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:43.240
Hungry!

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:45.810
Oh, sorry. Is it that time already?

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:49.110
I want to protect these children.

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:52.420
I want to create a world where these children can live with a smile.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:56.810
So I'm truly happy to gain an ally like you.

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:04.500
Say, Brother, are you another friend for us?

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:05.530
Well, uh...

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:07.230
What's your special technique?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.230
Special technique, huh...?

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:11.770
Afternoon naps, maybe?

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:14.160
This one's useless!

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:17.890
Afternoon naps are nice, aren't they?

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:20.630
Welcome home, Lafra!

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:23.740
I'm home. I like afternoon naps, too.

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:26.860
Welcome back, Lafra. It was just as you told me.

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:29.330
Ryner was in an Estabul inn.

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.950
It's a pleasure to meet you, Ryner Lute.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:38.770
My eyes are called Ebra Crypt.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.840
They replace the dreams in my head with those of other people.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.270
Basically, it's a power that resonates with people's dreams,

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.900
and allows me to see inside them.

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.100
So you saw my dreams?

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:55.940
What manner of unfulfilled dreams has such a hideous monster seen?

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:03.240
Sorry. All I can see are bits and pieces.

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:04.850
So...

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.600
Nah, don't worry about it.

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:09.620
That's how you found me?

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:14.720
Yes. Actually, I've been watching you for a rather long time now.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:18.050
But I never told Tiir or our friends that.

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:19.380
Why?

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.760
Because you were special.

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:25.900
You were completely different from other bearers of the Eyes of God.

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:29.070
I was fascinated by you.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.640
You're really kind.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:35.880
I kept watching your dreams.

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:39.910
Negative emotions so strong that they made me, an onlooker, want to cry and sob...

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:44.870
Anger, sorrow, hatred, despair...

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:49.710
Treated like dirt, feared, growing more and more, ever more lonely.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:54.170
Being afraid of hurting others. Being afraid of getting hurt.

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:57.590
Wishing you were dead, wishing you could go mad,

00:17:57.590 --> 00:17:59.930
being tormented by such feelings.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:07.400
And yet, what ultimately dominated your mind was the cry that you loved people.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:13.650
You always ultimately desire to protect those dear to you.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.680
You're sick of being alone.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:20.250
You love people. You love everyone.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.610
You may be a monster, but still,

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:28.180
you want more, more and more, to mingle with people.

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:36.590
You're so kind, so weak, so lonely, it makes me sad.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:40.700
Don't say that stuff with a face like you're gonna cry.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:45.590
Calling other people lonely and stuff?

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:49.810
Isn't everything you just said really about you?

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:53.490
That's why I called you here.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:56.100
Because I wanted salvation.

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:58.320
You wanted salvation?

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:00.480
For Tiir.

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:03.110
For the children here.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.700
For our friends gathered in the central continent.

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:13.590
And for yourself, Ryner.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:20.530
For the sad bearers of the Eyes of God, who have lost faith in humans.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:28.190
I want you to save them all. Because it's something I can't do.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:38.460
Dig in, okay, Lafra?

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:39.150
Thanks.

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:42.200
No fair giving brother Lafra all the attention!

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.990
Sister Pueka loves brother Lafra!

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:46.950
Love, love, love, love!

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:50.160
Come on, now, mind your manners!
Love, love, love, love!

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:50.180
Love, love, love, love!

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.150
Okay!

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:52.720
Sorry!

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:06.170
Eyes of God, huh?

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:10.370
Ryner, we're not humans, inferior creatures.

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:12.430
We are superior beings that bear the Eyes of God.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.010
<i>Is that really true?</i>

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:18.780
<i>Are we really monsters that are different from humans?</i>

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:21.950
<i>Can we really not get along with humans?</i>

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:26.350
<i>Isn't this the same thing? Nothing's different at all!</i>

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:30.570
<i>It's not like... It's not like...</i>

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:34.200
<i>It's not like we want these eyes, either!</i>

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:38.380
They're monsters whose very existence causes trouble.

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:45.510
For the sad bearers of the Eyes of God, who have lost faith in humans.

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:48.300
I want you to save them all.

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:51.250
<i>Me, save everyone?</i>

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:54.430
<i>I'm a cursed monster.</i>

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.490
<i>There's nothing to be gained from being saved at this point.</i>

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:00.810
<i>But they're different.</i>

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.400
<i>If they're labeled as monsters just for having their eyes,</i>

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:08.530
<i>does that mean there's nothing to be gained from saving any of us?</i>

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.730
<i>Is that really acceptable?</i>

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:24.430
Come on out.

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:32.390
As expected, the one known as Roland's most powerful magician is quite good.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:33.930
Who are...?

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:37.990
I'm the executive officer of the Taboo Breaker Pursuit Squadron, Callaud Squad.

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:40.350
Sergeant Luke Stokkart.

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:43.490
As ordered by His Majesty, Sion Astal,

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:47.850
Ryner Lute, I shall kill you.

00:23:21.680 --> 00:23:26.130
<i>I left Roland because I didn't want to make things suck for everyone.</i>

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:29.700
<i>Yet, why? Why do things end up this way?</i>

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:31.630
<i>Nobody wanted this.</i>

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:34.400
<i>Why does it end up sucking this much?!</i>
